  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 94872708bfe9e4851981e9e1837f1ac3, type: 3}
  m_Name: Caeser
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  exhibitName: Caeser's bust
  description: "Gaius Julius Caesar (12 or 13 July 100 BC \u2013 15 March 44 BC)
    was a Roman general and statesman. He was also an accomplished author and historian.
    A member of the First Triumvirate, Caesar led the Roman armies in the Gallic
    Wars before defeating his political rival Pompey in a civil war. He subsequently
    became dictator from 49 BC until his assassination in 44 BC. Caesar played a
    critical role in the events that led to the demise of the Roman Republic and
    the rise of the Roman Empire. \nThis bust made by Nicolas Coustou, a French Baroque
    sculptor, was created between 1658 and 1733. It was commissioned for the Gardens
    of Versailles and later moved to the Tuileries Garden before being acquired by
    the Louvre, where it is now displayed in the Cour Puget. "
  images: []
